Properties
/ Stage 3 — write each step's actions: which of its menu, in what order, how many times, and with
/ what property values.
/
/ This one IS an LLM call, not a decider question: order and property values are written, not
/ picked from a closed set. One request for the whole goal, because the steps refer to each other —
/ `%!data%` means the action before it, and a model shown one step alone cannot see that.
/
/ The answer is in the .pr's own action shape, so the step reads it through the same door it reads
/ a built .pr through — nothing converts it on the way in.

- render template "/system/builder/llm/templates/propertiesUser.template", write to %propertiesUserMsg%
- render template "/system/builder/llm/Properties.llm", write to %propertiesSystemMsg%
- render template "/system/builder/llm/Properties.schema", write to %propertiesSchema%
- set %messages% = [{"Role":"system", "Content":"%propertiesSystemMsg%"}, {"Role":"user", "Content":"%propertiesUserMsg%"}]

- llm.query Message=%messages%, Model="gpt-5.4-nano", Schema=%propertiesSchema%, cache=%!build.cache%, write to %properties%

- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goal-properties", goal=%goal%
